  "worked_solution": "From the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)=2$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}g(x)=4.$\n\nApplying the root and the quotient rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}\\sqrt{\\frac{3f(x)-g(x)}{f(x)}} & =\\sqrt{\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}\\frac{3f(x)-g(x)}{f(x)}\\,} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\,\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(3f(x)-g(x))}{{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)}\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator separately. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(3f(x)-g(x)) & =3(2)-4 \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)=2.\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}\\sqrt{\\frac{3f(x)-g(x)}{f(x)}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
